Here is the root cause:
When a process opens a ublk block device (e.g., to read the partition table), it holds disk->open_mutex. The read I/O completion path (blk_update_request or blk_mq_end_request) can trigger fput() on the block device file descriptor, which may be deferred to the same task's task work. This eventually calls blkdev_release(), which tries to acquire disk->open_mutex again, causing a deadlock since the mutex is already held by the same task.

Here is the patch:

+static void ublk_end_request(struct request *req, blk_status_t error)
+{
+	local_bh_disable();
+	blk_mq_end_request(req, error);
+	local_bh_enable();
+}
